WEBVTT

00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:07.875
[Riley echoing]
If I'm good at hockey,

00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:10.166
-I'll have friends.
-[chuckles]

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.625
[crackles]

00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:15.666
[warbles weakly]

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.791
[indistinct shouting]

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:18.166
[player grunts]

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:19.375
Whoo!

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:20.458
-Yeah!
-Okay, Miss Riley.

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:21.833
-Way to go, Michigan.
-Nice one, Michigan.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
All right, ladies.
Great day today.

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:25.625
Take it easy tonight.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.333
Yes! This is the moment
we've been waiting for.

00:00:28.416 --> 00:00:30.958
Party time with Val
and our future besties!

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:33.625
Why are we stopping?
What's going on?

00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:35.375
[Dani] There it is.

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:37.208
The red notebook.

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:39.666
Don't say it like that.
You'll freak her out.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.958
Why would it freak me out?

00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:42.250
Mmm, only because everything

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.791
Coach thinks about you
is in there.

00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:45.708
The good and the bad.

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:48.000
Whether she wants you
on the team...

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:49.708
-Or not.
-You guys, too much.

00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:52.500
-What? It's the truth.
-[chuckles] She's not wrong.

00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:54.416
What do you think
she's written about us?

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.250
I don't know.
Do you think it's bad?

00:00:56.416 --> 00:00:58.500
Well, I didn't until now!

00:00:58.583 --> 00:00:59.833
What if she's made
a list of

00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:01.208
all her favorite players,
and we're not on it?

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:02.750
Or a list of
all the worst players,

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:03.833
and we're at the top?

00:01:03.916 --> 00:01:05.541
Or worse,
we're not on either list,

00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:08.000
and we fade into obscurity!

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.541
Uh, sorry to interrupt you,
but they're walking away.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:11.708
[Anxiety exclaims]
We're losing them,

00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:12.833
we're losing them.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.541
[Anxiety] Okay.
First big hang with the group.

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:18.666
We just gotta act casual.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.041
Uh, why do our arms swing
like that when we walk?

00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:22.375
[Envy] Try to keep them still.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.541
[Anxiety] That looks crazy.
[Envy] Okay.

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:27.041
[Envy] Well, walk like Dani.
Her arms have rhythm.

00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:29.458
[Anxiety]
No, you're making it worse!

00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:30.708
[Envy] Well,
that wasn't my intention.

00:01:30.791 --> 00:01:32.458
I'm sorry
for trying something!

00:01:32.541 --> 00:01:34.541
[Ennui] Uh, what do you think
pockets are for?

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:35.666
[Envy] Oh, that's good.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.083
[Anxiety] Ennui,
I am very proud of you.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:38.500
[all laughing]

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:39.625
[Envy] What are they
laughing about?

00:01:39.791 --> 00:01:41.458
Does anybody know
what cool people laugh about?

00:01:41.541 --> 00:01:43.125
I don't know. We were too
focused on the arms thing.

00:01:43.208 --> 00:01:44.791
Just pretend we get the joke.

00:01:44.875 --> 00:01:46.083
[laughs]

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.291
[Embarrassment groans]

00:01:51.958 --> 00:01:54.750
[Fear] Joy, Anger is
taking up the floret.

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:56.250
Fear, what is the matter
with you?

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.541
I don't like this vessel.

00:01:57.625 --> 00:01:58.625
Well, that's all we have.

00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:00.125
How much longer
till we get there?

00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:01.375
We'll get there
when we get there.

00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:03.916
I bet Anxiety would know
how long, down to the minute.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.833
Well, she just knows
everything, doesn't she?

00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:07.041
Look,
I don't like her words,

00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:08.375
and I do not like her actions.

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:09.791
I just think I can change her.

00:02:09.875 --> 00:02:12.208
You know what?
Who likes banana bread?

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:13.541
Show of hands.

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:14.666
[indistinct conversation]

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:19.500
So, Michigan,
who's your favorite band?

00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.125
Uh...

00:02:21.208 --> 00:02:22.333
Everyone's staring at us.

00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:24.333
There's only one right answer
to this question.

00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:27.625
Oh! Get Up and Glow!
They're so awesome.

00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:29.166
Get Up and Glow!

00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:31.666
I was all over them
in middle school.

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:32.833
-[Dani] Are you serious?
-[Valentina] Yeah,

00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:34.666
I was a Glow Girly. Relax.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.000
No! We need a band
they think is cool,

00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:38.375
not one we actually like.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.375
Quick, recall everything
we know about music.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.916
[whirring]

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:44.375
Uh-oh!

00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:46.958
[Sadness screaming]

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.750
[grunts]

00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:50.458
[grunting]

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.083
[screaming]

00:02:56.791 --> 00:02:59.125
We have to know
one cool song, right?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.500
-[Sadness grunts]
-[memories clattering]

00:03:01.583 --> 00:03:03.416
-[man] ♪ TripleDent gum ♪
-[woman] ♪ Will make you smile ♪

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.750
Embarrassment,
get that out of there!

00:03:04.916 --> 00:03:06.000
Come on, there's gotta be
something in here.

00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:07.083
[Envy] I'm looking,
I'm looking.

00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:08.166
[Anxiety] Something better,
something cool. Come on.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.416
No, not that. No.

00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:12.041
This is the best we have!

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:14.750
It's mostly jingles
and Dad's yacht rock.

00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:16.791
But, I mean,
you don't still like

00:03:16.875 --> 00:03:18.416
Get Up and Glow, do you?

00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:20.583
Okay, don't panic.
What do we do?

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:21.791
If we don't like their music,

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:22.916
we have nothing

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.041
-to offer these girls.
-[Ennui groans]

00:03:24.125 --> 00:03:25.125
We'll be outed as the imposter

00:03:25.208 --> 00:03:26.416
-that we obviously are.
-Pardon. Excusez moi.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.416
I've been waiting my whole
life for this very moment.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.500
[console buzzes]

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:34.041
[sarcastically] Oh, yeah.
I love Get Up and Glow.

00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:36.541
[echoing]
Love Get Up and Glow.

00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:39.875
[all screaming]

00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:40.958
[♪ intense music playing]

00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:44.375
Abandon broccoli!

00:03:44.458 --> 00:03:45.583
[Disgust screams]

00:03:46.208 --> 00:03:47.208
[Joy screams]

00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:50.875
[Joy breathing heavily]

00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:54.750
-[Disgust] Joy!
-Give us your hand! Come on.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.000
[both grunting]

00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:58.083
What is that?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.625
That's a Sar-chasm.

00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:01.208
It can open for miles!

00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:02.750
Run for your lives!

00:04:02.916 --> 00:04:05.041
Sar-chasm? Really?

00:04:05.208 --> 00:04:06.458
[Riley sarcastically]
Get Up and Glow

00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:07.791
is my favorite band.

00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:09.708
But she loves Get Up and Glow.

00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:11.291
They choreograph
their own dances.

00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:12.541
Okay, Joy,

00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:13.708
if we can't follow the stream,

00:04:13.791 --> 00:04:14.791
we don't know
where we're going.

00:04:14.875 --> 00:04:16.166
And if we don't know
where we're going,

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.666
we can't follow the stream!

00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:21.791
It is an endless loop
of tragedy and consequence!

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:23.541
Or we could just
ask those guys.

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:25.083
Oh, yeah. Or that.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.208
Boy, are we so lucky
we ran into you guys!

00:04:28.291 --> 00:04:31.416
[echoing in sarcastic voice]
Boy, are we so lucky

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.916
-we ran into you guys!
-Huh?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Please,
we really need your help!

00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:40.833
[echoing in sarcastic voice]
We really need your help.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.208
What's their problem?

00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:44.458
Guys, you just gotta
turn on the charm.

00:04:44.541 --> 00:04:45.833
[chuckles] Hey!

00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:47.375
[echoing in sarcastic voice]
I bet you're the best

00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:49.958
crane crew in the world!

00:04:50.125 --> 00:04:52.083
Wow, those guys are jerks.

00:04:53.708 --> 00:04:56.166
-Wow, those guys are jerks.
-[crane beeping]

00:04:56.333 --> 00:05:00.041
[sarcastically] Oh, yeah.
Get Up and Glow is so awesome.

00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:02.000
Riley, what are you
talking about?

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:04.250
-You love Get Up and Glow.
-Oh. Uh...

00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:05.666
-Hey, guys.
-[Envy groans]

00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:07.375
Why are our best friends

00:05:07.458 --> 00:05:09.000
always trying to
hang out with us?

00:05:09.166 --> 00:05:11.708
Come on, Riley,
we just went to their concert.

00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:12.875
Well, yeah.

00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:14.583
-I mean, sure, but like...
-But what?

00:05:14.666 --> 00:05:15.666
We had a great time.

00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:17.541
-Grace, you are not helping.
-[console buzzes]

00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:18.791
[sarcastically] Oh, yeah,

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.708
-we had a great time.
-[Fire Hawks exclaim]

00:05:20.791 --> 00:05:22.458
[Riley echoing] Great time.

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:24.333
[worker clamoring]

00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:26.083
Why can't they just
leave her alone?

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.791
What are we gonna do now, Joy?

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:30.166
We go the long way,
which is the best way.

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:32.666
Stretch those hammies, Anger.
Let's go.

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:35.416
Best night of my life.

00:05:35.583 --> 00:05:37.500
Well,
this has been really fun.

00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:38.791
Extremely.

00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:39.916
But we're gonna go now.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.500
Okay, bye.

00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:42.875
-[♪ upbeat pop music playing]
-Oh, this is

00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:44.000
the best band ever!

00:05:44.166 --> 00:05:46.083
-Okay, Riley!
-Michigan knows what's up!

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.416
See? As long as
we like what they like,

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.875
we have all the friends
we need.

00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:52.041
-[Riley laughing]
-[Sofia] Night, guys.

00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:54.166
Well, I think
I'm calling it a night.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.333
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, it's late.

00:05:56.416 --> 00:05:57.458
Plus, I think
you'll want to get some sleep

00:05:57.541 --> 00:05:58.541
before tomorrow's scrimmage.

00:05:58.625 --> 00:05:59.625
What scrimmage?

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:02.291
Uh. It's just something Coach
always does on the last day.

00:06:02.458 --> 00:06:04.083
It's how Val made the team
as a freshman.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.250
Don't tell her that.

00:06:05.416 --> 00:06:06.958
Val scored two goals.

00:06:07.041 --> 00:06:08.541
No freshman
has ever done that.

00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:09.625
Dani, stop.

00:06:09.791 --> 00:06:11.958
Technically, it's not your
tryout for the next year,

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:13.583
but it basically is.

00:06:14.375 --> 00:06:16.375
You'll do great.
Just be yourself.

00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:17.500
[Anxiety] Did you hear that?

00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:19.708
We could become a Fire Hawk,
like, tomorrow.

00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:22.958
But how do we be ourself if
our new self isn't ready yet?

00:06:23.041 --> 00:06:24.458
[grunts] Excellent point.

00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:26.500
Let's get
these memories downstairs.

00:06:26.583 --> 00:06:27.583
[memories clattering]

00:06:28.083 --> 00:06:29.083
Oh...

